  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nSee this comment for more context:\n\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/10956/files#r1944022348\n\nThere are a number of things listed in the [Flow Content section of Rendering](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#flow-content-3) that **a)** should stay together, so their relative order is preserved, but **b)** don't seem to belong in the Flow Content section of Rendering.\n\nPerhaps this subset of the stylesheet? These include the modifications being made in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/10956. Perhaps they should also include all of the styling of popovers and dialogs? I don't know.\n\n```css\ndialog:not([open]) {\n  display: none;\n}\n[popover]:not(:popover-open):not(dialog[open]) {\n  display:none;\n}\ndialog:popover-open {\n  display:block;\n}\n:modal {\n  interactivity: auto;\n}\n[inert] {\n  interactivity: inert;\n}\n```",
